.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-DEBIANUTILS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-debianutils ,
.Nm pipe_progress ,
.Nm run-parts ,
.Nm start-stop-daemon ,
.Nm which
.Nd BusyBox script and process utilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm pipe_progress
.Nm run-parts
.Op Fl a Ar ARG
.Ar ...
.Op Fl u Ar UMASK
.Op Fl -reverse
.Op Fl -test
.Op Fl -exit-on-error
.Op Fl -list
.Ar DIRECTORY
.Nm start-stop-daemon
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Brq Fl S | Fl K
.Ar ...
.Op Fl - Ar ARGS ...
.Nm which
.Op Fl a
.Ar COMMAND ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the debianutils applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width start-stop-daemon
.It Nm pipe_progress
Copy standard input to standard output, writing dots to standard error
to indicate activity.
.It Nm run-parts
Run scripts in
.Ar DIRECTORY .
.It Nm start-stop-daemon
Search for processes matching all specified conditions.
With
.Fl K ,
stop matching processes; with
.Fl S ,
start a process unless a match is found.
.It Nm which
Locate each
.Ar COMMAND .
With
.Fl a ,
show all matches.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss run-parts
.Bl -tag -width "--exit-on-error"
.It Fl a Ar ARG
Pass an argument to each script; may be repeated.
.It Fl u Ar UMASK
Set the file creation mask before running scripts.
.It Fl -reverse
Reverse execution order.
.It Fl -test
Show what would run without executing scripts.
.It Fl -exit-on-error
Exit if a script returns a nonzero status.
.It Fl -list
Print matching file names, including files that are not executable.
.El
.Ss start-stop-daemon
Process matching options:
.Bl -tag -width "-u USERNAME|UID"
.It Fl u Ar USERNAME|UID
Match only this user's processes.
.It Fl n Ar NAME
Match the command name in
.Pa /proc/PID/stat .
.It Fl x Ar EXECUTABLE
Match the command in
.Pa /proc/PID/cmdline .
.It Fl p Ar FILE
Match the process ID read from
.Ar FILE .
.El
.Pp
Options for starting a process with
.Fl S :
.Bl -tag -width "-x EXECUTABLE"
.It Fl x Ar EXECUTABLE
Program to run.
.It Fl a Ar NAME
Zeroth argument.
.It Fl b
Run in the background.
.It Fl N Ar N
Request a change in nice level.
Rach2 has no
.Fn setpriority
system call; this option fails before starting the program.
.It Fl c Ar USER Ns Op : Ns Op Ar GRP
Take the user's identity and supplementary groups, with the user's primary
group unless
.Ar GRP
names another.
.It Fl m
Write the process ID to the file specified by
.Fl p .
.El
.Pp
Options for stopping processes with
.Fl K :
.Bl -tag -width "-s SIG"
.It Fl s Ar SIG
Signal to send.
.It Fl t
Only match processes.
Without
.Fl o ,
the status is 0 when at least one process matches and can be signalled.
.El
.Pp
Other options:
.Bl -tag -width "-o"
.It Fl o
Return status 0 if nothing is done.
.It Fl v
Accepted but has no effect.
.It Fl q
Suppress output.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl which login
.Sh HISTORY
